sequenceDiagram
    participant Admin as Cluster Admin
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant DSCCtrl as DSC Controller<br/>Manager Pod
    participant DSCICtrl as DSCI Controller<br/>Manager Pod
    participant ModReconciler as Module Reconciler<br/>Manager Pod
    participant GWCtrl as Gateway Controller<br/>Manager Pod
    participant Webhook as Webhook Server<br/>9443/TCP HTTPS
    participant CompOps as Component Operator Pods
    participant EnvoyGW as Envoy Gateway<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant AuthProxy as kube-auth-proxy<br/>OIDC TLS
    participant Backend as Backend Service

    Note over Admin,Backend: Flow 1: Component Enablement via DataScienceCluster
    Admin->>K8sAPI: kubectl apply DataScienceCluster<br/>Auth: kubeconfig
    K8sAPI->>Webhook: POST /validate-datasciencecluster-v2<br/>HTTPS TLS (service-ca)
    Webhook-->>K8sAPI: Admission Response (allow/deny)
    K8sAPI->>Webhook: POST /mutate-datasciencecluster-v2<br/>HTTPS TLS (service-ca)
    Webhook-->>K8sAPI: Mutated DSC
    K8sAPI->>DSCCtrl: Watch event: DSC created/updated<br/>ServiceAccount token
    DSCCtrl->>DSCCtrl: Evaluate enabled components<br/>DAG-based reconciliation
    DSCCtrl->>ModReconciler: Trigger module reconciliation
    ModReconciler->>ModReconciler: Render kustomize manifests<br/>/opt/manifests-template<br/>Apply RELATED_IMAGE_* overrides
    ModReconciler->>K8sAPI: Apply component Deployments<br/>HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    K8sAPI->>CompOps: Create component operator pods

    Note over Admin,Backend: Flow 1b: Platform Initialization via DSCInitialization
    Admin->>K8sAPI: kubectl apply DSCInitialization<br/>Auth: kubeconfig
    K8sAPI->>DSCICtrl: Watch event: DSCI created<br/>ServiceAccount token
    DSCICtrl->>K8sAPI: Create application namespace<br/>HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    DSCICtrl->>K8sAPI: Configure monitoring resources<br/>HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    DSCICtrl->>K8sAPI: Setup service mesh integration<br/>HTTPS TLS 1.2+

    Note over Admin,Backend: Flow 2: Platform Ingress via Gateway API
    participant User as External User

    User->>EnvoyGW: HTTPS request to platform<br/>443/TCP TLS 1.2+
    EnvoyGW->>EnvoyGW: HTTPRoute matching<br/>EnvoyFilter: auth header injection
    EnvoyGW->>AuthProxy: Forward to kube-auth-proxy<br/>HTTPS TLS (self-signed + DestinationRule)
    AuthProxy->>AuthProxy: OIDC token validation<br/>OpenID Connect provider
    AuthProxy->>Backend: Forward authenticated request<br/>Inject auth headers
    Backend-->>AuthProxy: Response
    AuthProxy-->>EnvoyGW: Response
    EnvoyGW-->>User: HTTPS Response
